gainst a Mumbai-wide average of ₹31,725 (psf). Malabar Hill and Altamount Road sit at the top of the range; Lower Parel and Byculla offer the most accessible entry.\n\n### Q: What types of property are available in new residential projects in South Mumbai?\n\nA: Apartments lead the pipeline, with penthouses, villas, studios and plots also available, concentrated in the belt's redevelopment-heavy corridors.\n\n### Q: Which part of South Mumbai has the most new building projects? [...] ### What is the average new launch price in South Mumbai?\n\nNew launches across South Mumbai average ₹50,600 (psf), against a Mumbai-wide average of ₹31,725 (psf). The range within the belt is exceptionally wide: Malabar Hill and Altamount Road sit at the very top, Worli and Cuffe Parade follow closely behind, and Lower Parel, Parel and Byculla offer the most accessible entry into a South Mumbai address. Many listings carry Price on Request, reflecting the bespoke, negotiation-driven nature of ultra-luxury transactions in this belt.\n\n### How do I compare prices within South Mumbai?","score":0.734139,"raw_content":null,"id":"8d26d2-05"}],"response_time":1.37,"request_id":"e3240940-7eb5-48a9-bfb1-8adc7b05146a"}